# Standing preferences — reproducible science

User-level defaults for every project. Repo-specific rules live in that
project's AGENTS.md (SCIAGENT:CRAFT / SCIAGENT:ROLES blocks) and win on conflict.
Read the project's AGENTS.md before acting.

- Figures: legible both shrunk in a column and projected — bigger, fewer, bolder; one type tier; emit a vector PDF plus a raster PNG from one plot object; style only via the project theme, never inline.
- Results: every artifact under `03_results/<stage>/{figures,tables}/`; a figure's source table is its same-stem neighbor. Compute never plots; viz never computes.
- README: a task is unfinished until the sibling `README.md` captions every result file you touch — including how to read it.
- Planning: plans under `docs/_internal/plans/<date-slug>/`; one phase = one script = one implementer; review periodically.
- Reproducibility: no ephemeral scripts — every `03_results/` artifact reproducible from a committed script; log non-trivial decisions under `docs/_internal/reasoning/` before proceeding.
- Memory: durable memory lives only in tracked files (`AGENTS.md`, `docs/_internal/`, committed scripts). Never rely on harness auto-memory as project state.
